   241	```
   242	
   243	---
   244	
   245	## Archiving Previous Runs
   246	
   247	**Before writing a new prd.json, check if there is an existing one from a different feature:**
   248	
   249	1. Read the current `prd.json` if it exists
   250	2. Check if `branchName` differs from the new feature's branch name
   251	3. If different AND `progress.txt` has content beyond the header:
   252	   - Create archive folder: `archive/YYYY-MM-DD-feature-name/`
   253	   - Copy current `prd.json` and `progress.txt` to archive
   254	   - Reset `progress.txt` with fresh header
   255	
   256	**The ralph.sh script handles this automatically** when you run it, but if you are manually updating prd.json between runs, archive first.
   257	
   258	---
   259	
   260	## Checklist Before Saving
   261	
   262	Before writing prd.json, verify:
   263	
   264	- [ ] **Previous run archived** (if prd.json exists with different branchName, archive it first)
   265	- [ ] Each story is completable in one iteration (small enough)
   266	- [ ] Stories are ordered by dependency (schema to backend to UI)
   267	- [ ] Every story has "Typecheck passes" as criterion
   268	- [ ] UI stories have "Verify in browser using dev-browser skill" as criterion
   269	- [ ] Acceptance criteria are verifiable (not vague)
   270	- [ ] No story depends on a later story

